{"issue":{"title":"Add a --shout option to greet and document it in docs/","problem":"bin/greet.js has no --shout option. It picks the first argument that does not start with '--' as the name and silently ignores every '--' flag, so `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `Hello, Ada!` exactly like the plain call. src/greet.js only exports `greeting(name)` returning `Hello, ${name}!`. docs/index.md, which .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes to https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ on every push to main, documents only `node bin/greet.js <name>` and does not mention --shout.","reason":"Support wants a louder greeting for the lobby screen and wants a docs page they can point people to. Right now the flag is accepted but does nothing, so users get no error and no shouted greeting.","outcome":"`greet --shout <name>` prints the greeting in upper case. Without the flag the output is unchanged. docs/index.md documents --shout, so the existing pages workflow puts it on the published site once the PR merges.","expect":["`node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` exits 0 and prints exactly `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline on stdout","`node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) also exits 0 and prints exactly `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline","`node bin/greet.js Ada` without the flag still prints exactly `Hello, Ada!` followed by a newline","`node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with status 2 and writes the usage message to stderr, as the plain no-name call does","docs/index.md documents the --shout option, showing its usage and that it prints the greeting in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, <NAME>!`)","The test suite has at least one test that runs bin/greet.js with --shout and asserts the upper-case output, and `npm test` passes"],"proofs":[{"line":"`node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` exits 0 and prints exactly `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline on stdout","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js --shout Ada | od -c; echo exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]} — expect `HELLO, ADA!\\n` and exit=0"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) also exits 0 and prints exactly `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ada --shout | od -c; echo exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]} — expect `HELLO, ADA!\\n` and exit=0"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js Ada` without the flag still prints exactly `Hello, Ada!` followed by a newline","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ada | od -c — expect `Hello, Ada!\\n`"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with status 2 and writes the usage message to stderr, as the plain no-name call does","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js --shout; echo exit=$? — expect `usage: greet <name>` (or updated usage that mentions --shout) on stderr, nothing on stdout, exit=2"},{"line":"docs/index.md documents the --shout option, showing its usage and that it prints the greeting in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, <NAME>!`)","proof":"read","how":"Read docs/index.md at the PR head: it must show an invocation that uses --shout and say that the output is the upper-case greeting"},{"line":"The test suite has at least one test that runs bin/greet.js with --shout and asserts the upper-case output, and `npm test` passes","proof":"run","how":"Read test/ for a test that runs bin/greet.js with --shout and asserts `HELLO, ADA!` (or the upper-case greeting for another name), then run `npm test` and expect `# fail 0`"}],"non_goals":["Confirming that the live site https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ shows the change. That only happens after merge, when the existing pages workflow deploys docs/.","Changing .github/workflows/pages.yml or how the docs are published","Adding other options, such as a short alias like -s, colours, or extra punctuation","Rejecting or validating other unknown '--' flags"],"assumptions":["'Louder' means the whole greeting in upper case, punctuation kept: `HELLO, ADA!` for Ada","The flag can go before or after the name","Making it 'show up on the published docs site' means documenting it in docs/index.md, which the existing pages workflow publishes from main. The PR can only be checked on docs/index.md itself.","How to implement it (for example a new option on `greeting` in src/greet.js versus upper-casing in bin/greet.js) is the builder's choice. Only the CLI behaviour is required.","README.md does not need to change, since it only links to the docs site"]}}